        <name>context</name>
        <briefdescription>
<para>The owning context. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>This is the context in which the pointer itself was created. For a member variable, it is the same as the context of the containing object. Because the containing object holds a <ref refid="classlibbirch_1_1WeakPtr" kindref="compound">WeakPtr</ref> to the same object, use of an <ref refid="classlibbirch_1_1InitPtr" kindref="compound">InitPtr</ref> is sufficient here. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
